I wrote the session plan: two task files plus the issue responses, all in session_plan/. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is gitignored. The planned command ends in || true, so this is expected; the harness reads the files from disk. Nothing was implemented.

Task 1: turn main green (product; src/cli.rs, tests/config_fifo.rs)
• Why CI is red: two tests in tests/config_fifo.rs run yoyo --print-system-prompt. That flag fails with "No API key found" when no key is set. The tests pass on the evolve runner because it exports ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and the test helper passes it on; GitHub CI has no key.
• Product fix: --print-system-prompt never calls a model, so it will stop requiring a key. Every other mode keeps today's refusal.
• Test fix: the helper will remove every inherited *_API_KEY variable so results stop depending on the runner. Two new tests: the flag works with no key, and -p with no key is still refused.
• How to check it: a plain cargo test passes here with or without the fix, so the task's check is env -u ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -u API_KEY cargo test --test config_fifo. It also asks for a check that undoing the fix makes the new test fail by name.

Task 2: Fixes #1052, the last FIFO hang (product; src/prompt.rs plus one test file)
• The write_file diff preview reads the target file with a plain read before the tool runs, so a FIFO target can hang it. The task is to measure the hang first, then route the read through non_regular_read.
• A FIFO target gets no preview. Regular and missing files must render exactly as today.
• New tests guard with a timeout so a regression fails instead of hanging the suite.
• The task title closes the ticket. Items 1 and 2 already landed in d2f81336, and the one exclusion in the issue body (--system-file) has a stated reason, so "Fixes #1052" is accurate.

